# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# build output
/bin/
/bootstrap
/lambda.zip

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Terraform
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform-tmp/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
crash.log

# Generated API reference (make docs)
docs/api.html

# Bruno environments hold credentials. Marking a variable "secret" in Bruno
# keeps its value out of the .bru file, but that is a checkbox someone has to
# remember - and a non-secret variable is written into the file verbatim. So
# the files are ignored outright and only .example versions are shared.
bruno/environments/*.bru
!bruno/environments/*.bru.example

# A saved plan contains every attribute value in plaintext, secrets included.
tfplan
*.tfplan
